From c636eda10aac7677fc26e66587b301b8659f0258 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:32:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion): Parallel finish crosses a hole narrower than
 the ball

The raster line broke at each hole rim, because no facet answers under
the ball centre there. Each hole, also one that the ball cannot enter,
gave a retract and a plunge. A lid step a hair off the rim did the same.

bridge_line now joins two pieces of one raster line with one straight
feed when the gap is not wider than the ball (2r), the slope is not
steeper than 45 degrees, and the swept ball stays clear of each facet by
r minus the chord budget (dist_seg_tri, as column_clear does). A hole
that the ball fits into keeps its hop.

swarf, swarf_multi and norm_dir move from raster.rs to swarf.rs, so that
raster.rs stays under 400 lines.

Fixes #2431

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
